{"voice":"IKne3meq5aSn9XLyUdCD","model":"eleven_v3","chunks":[{"audio":"/audio-chapters/3.3-1.mp3","steps":[{"key":"intro","text":"Chapter 3.3: Revenue, Costs and Profit. Let's read it together, and I'll explain each part as we go.","words":[[0.271,0.411],[0.571,2.091],[2.161,2.651],[2.798,3.531],[3.611,3.851],[3.92,4.411],[4.631,5.371],[5.403,5.531],[5.558,5.611],[5.664,6.251],[6.291,6.411],[6.451,6.571],[6.621,6.971],[7.035,7.291],[7.355,7.611],[7.718,7.931],[7.984,8.091],[8.171,8.731]]},{"key":"canvas#0","text":"The money side of the canvas","words":[[9.231,9.531],[9.584,9.851],[9.947,10.331],[10.411,10.571],[10.591,10.651],[10.72,11.131]]},{"key":"canvas#1","text":"In plain words Revenue streams are how money comes in. The cost structure is where it goes out. Profit is what is left when the first is bigger than the second.","words":[[11.718,12.251],[12.318,12.651],[12.718,13.051],[13.141,13.771],[13.831,14.251],[14.311,14.491],[14.551,14.731],[14.784,15.051],[15.118,15.451],[15.558,16.011],[16.211,16.811],[16.891,17.211],[17.259,17.691],[17.771,17.931],[17.958,18.091],[18.144,18.251],[18.299,18.491],[18.571,19.051],[19.222,20.251],[20.358,20.571],[20.603,20.731],[20.784,20.891],[20.971,21.291],[21.339,21.531],[21.551,21.611],[21.691,22.091],[22.198,22.411],[22.468,22.811],[22.859,23.051],[23.091,23.211],[23.268,23.611]]},{"key":"canvas#explain","text":"Here's the idea: Now we reach the money side of the canvas: revenue streams and cost structure.","words":[[25.004,25.132],[25.152,25.212],[25.308,26.412],[26.492,26.732],[26.785,26.892],[26.959,27.292],[27.332,27.452],[27.505,27.772],[27.836,28.092],[28.119,28.172],[28.192,28.252],[28.332,29.372],[29.432,29.852],[29.912,30.332],[30.412,30.652],[30.732,31.052],[31.108,32.012]]},{"key":"revenue#0","text":"How money comes in","words":[[32.512,32.812],[32.865,33.132],[33.185,33.452],[33.559,33.772]]},{"key":"revenue#1","text":"Direct sales on the website","words":[[34.549,35.132],[35.199,35.532],[35.559,35.612],[35.652,35.772],[35.872,36.572]]},{"key":"revenue#2","text":"Customers buy straight from the brand.","words":[[36.732,37.452],[37.512,37.692],[37.745,38.172],[38.22,38.412],[38.432,38.492],[38.559,38.892]]},{"key":"revenue#3","text":"Amazon · Blinkit · Zepto · Instamart","words":[[38.996,39.613],[39.813,40.013],[40.066,40.413],[40.613,40.813],[40.866,41.373],[41.573,41.773],[41.821,42.333]]},{"key":"revenue#4","text":"Sales through marketplaces and quick commerce","words":[[43.36,44.093],[44.123,44.333],[44.39,45.133],[45.213,45.453],[45.493,45.693],[45.755,46.253]]},{"key":"revenue#5","text":"Customers buy on someone else’s platform, which keeps a share.","words":[[46.677,47.613],[47.713,48.013],[48.066,48.173],[48.223,48.573],[48.653,49.053],[49.124,49.773],[49.84,50.173],[50.213,50.413],[50.453,50.493],[50.56,50.973]]},{"key":"revenue#6","text":"Corporate gifting and bulk orders","words":[[51.897,52.653],[52.693,53.133],[53.213,53.453],[53.501,53.693],[53.75,54.093]]},{"key":"revenue#7","text":"Companies buy many boxes at once.","words":[[54.509,55.373],[55.433,55.613],[55.693,56.013],[56.093,56.493],[56.52,56.573],[56.669,57.173]]},{"key":"revenue#8","text":"These are the four categories revenue is reported by. No split between them is published in this chapter.","words":[[57.44,58.173],[58.193,58.253],[58.313,58.493],[58.525,58.653],[58.726,59.453],[59.513,59.933],[59.986,60.093],[60.146,60.573],[60.68,61.133],[61.4,61.933],[62,62.333],[62.383,62.733],[62.765,62.893],[62.92,62.973],[63.021,63.453],[63.506,63.613],[63.645,63.773],[63.823,64.253]]},{"key":"revenue#9","text":"In plain words A revenue stream is one way of earning. Looking at revenue by channel and by category shows which parts of the business bring in the most.","words":[[64.76,65.293],[65.36,65.693],[65.76,66.093],[66.293,66.493],[66.543,66.893],[66.95,67.293],[67.4,67.613],[67.693,67.933],[68.013,68.253],[68.333,68.493],[68.553,69.213],[69.333,70.173],[70.2,70.253],[70.313,70.733],[70.813,70.973],[71.033,71.453],[71.533,71.773],[71.826,71.933],[72.013,72.653],[72.746,73.213],[73.253,73.453],[73.52,73.853],[73.88,73.933],[73.953,74.013],[74.066,74.493],[74.546,74.813],[74.866,74.973],[74.993,75.053],[75.149,75.613]]},{"key":"revenue#explain","text":"In simple words: Revenue streams are the ways money comes in, like sales on the brand's website, on marketplaces and quick commerce apps, and corporate gifting orders.","words":[[76.706,76.813],[76.87,77.213],[77.28,77.693],[77.813,78.653],[78.723,79.213],[79.253,79.373],[79.413,79.533],[79.613,79.933],[80,80.333],[80.386,80.653],[80.76,81.533],[81.581,81.773],[81.84,82.173],[82.2,82.253],[82.273,82.333],[82.386,82.733],[82.803,83.773],[83.826,83.933],[84.002,84.813],[84.913,85.213],[85.266,85.533],[85.577,85.933],[86.013,86.413],[86.553,86.973],[87.021,87.453],[87.493,87.853],[87.91,88.333]]},{"key":"costs#0","text":"Where the money goes","words":[[89.266,89.933],[89.973,90.093],[90.146,90.413],[90.525,90.973]]},{"key":"costs#1","text":"1 Ingredients and production","words":[[91.933,92.413],[92.5,93.453],[93.533,93.773],[93.817,94.253]]},{"key":"costs#2","text":"2 Packaging","words":[[95.293,95.533],[95.661,96.813]]},{"key":"costs#3","text":"3 Logistics and delivery","words":[[97.693,98.013],[98.133,99.213],[99.273,99.453],[99.515,100.013]]},{"key":"costs#4","text":"4 Marketing and platform commissions","words":[[100.973,101.293],[101.413,102.493],[102.533,102.653],[102.724,103.293],[103.346,103.933]]},{"key":"costs#5","text":"5 Team, kitchen and operating costs","words":[[104.893,105.373],[105.549,106.333],[106.423,107.053],[107.153,107.453],[107.501,107.933],[108.026,108.493]]},{"key":"costs#6","text":"In plain words Every order carries these costs. Some are paid per order (ingredients, packaging, delivery, commission ). Others, like the team and the kitchen, are paid whether or not an order comes in.","words":[[109.133,109.773],[109.84,110.173],[110.253,110.653],[110.773,111.373],[111.44,111.773],[111.843,112.333],[112.373,112.573],[112.666,113.453],[113.565,114.013],[114.053,114.173],[114.237,114.493],[114.573,114.813],[114.88,115.213],[115.533,116.813],[116.861,117.693],[117.746,118.493],[118.558,119.213],[119.506,120.093],[120.15,120.733],[120.765,120.893],[120.933,121.053],[121.133,121.453],[121.493,121.613],[121.633,121.693],[121.743,122.413],[122.453,122.573],[122.653,122.973],[123.013,123.293],[123.346,123.453],[123.553,123.853],[123.906,124.013],[124.066,124.333],[124.386,124.653],[124.76,125.333]]},{"key":"costs#explain","text":"Think of it like this: The cost structure is where money goes out: ingredients, packaging, logistics, marketing, and the team and kitchen.","words":[[125.826,125.859],[125.886,125.939],[125.992,126.099],[126.147,126.339],[126.419,127.299],[127.319,127.379],[127.459,127.779],[127.827,128.259],[128.339,128.499],[128.552,128.819],[128.872,129.139],[129.203,129.459],[129.519,130.259],[130.319,131.299],[131.347,132.179],[132.243,133.219],[133.267,134.099],[134.139,134.259],[134.279,134.339],[134.435,134.819],[134.879,135.059],[135.109,135.539]]},{"key":"profit#0","text":"Growing fast, not yet in profit","words":[[136.529,137.299],[137.411,138.099],[138.199,138.499],[138.579,138.819],[138.899,139.059],[139.128,139.539]]},{"key":"profit#1","text":"Common for a fast-growing brand that invests in growth.","words":[[139.939,140.899],[140.939,141.059],[141.099,141.139],[141.235,142.019],[142.099,142.499],[142.531,142.659],[142.728,143.219],[143.246,143.299],[143.356,143.779]]},{"key":"profit#2","text":"Reported FY24 revenue was about Rs 14.7 crore , up around 165% from about Rs 5.5 crore in FY23. The business reported a net loss of about Rs 63 lakh for FY24, which is common for a fast-growing brand that invests in growth.","words":[[144.357,145.139],[145.326,146.179],[146.249,146.739],[146.799,146.979],[147.032,147.299],[147.312,147.339],[147.379,148.579],[148.632,148.899],[149.419,149.939],[149.992,150.099],[150.156,150.499],[150.579,152.259],[152.355,152.739],[152.779,152.979],[153.032,153.139],[153.339,154.019],[154.072,154.339],[154.632,155.219],[155.379,156.899],[157.039,157.459],[157.512,157.939],[158.001,158.499],[158.579,158.659],[158.739,158.979],[159.075,159.459],[159.486,159.539],[159.592,159.859],[159.886,159.939],[160.019,160.659],[160.739,161.059],[161.239,161.779],[161.992,163.699],[163.726,163.859],[163.912,164.019],[164.065,164.339],[164.399,164.579],[164.619,164.659],[164.739,165.459],[165.539,165.939],[166.003,166.259],[166.339,166.899],[166.926,166.979],[167.036,167.459]]},{"key":"profit#3","text":"the cost of making it and of delivering it","words":[[167.819,168.659],[168.723,168.979],[169.032,169.139],[169.185,169.459],[169.539,169.699],[169.799,170.099],[170.152,170.259],[170.303,170.739],[170.792,170.899]]},{"key":"profit#4","text":"In plain words Unit economics means looking at what one order earns after the cost of making and delivering it.","words":[[171.379,171.859],[171.926,172.259],[172.339,172.739],[172.899,173.539],[173.603,174.179],[174.232,174.499],[174.539,174.819],[174.872,174.979],[175.027,175.219],[175.319,175.619],[175.686,176.019],[176.112,176.579],[176.686,177.219],[177.239,177.299],[177.379,177.699],[177.752,177.859],[177.928,178.339],[178.439,178.739],[178.783,179.219],[179.272,179.459]]},{"key":"profit#explain","text":"So what does that mean? Profit is what is left when money in is bigger than money out. Eat Better's sales grew fast, from about five and a half crore rupees to about fourteen point seven crore rupees, while the business was still working towards profit.","words":[[180.632,180.739],[180.803,181.059],[181.107,181.299],[181.331,181.459],[181.555,182.579],[182.67,183.219],[183.299,183.459],[183.491,183.619],[183.672,183.779],[183.859,184.179],[184.211,184.339],[184.392,184.659],[184.792,185.059],[185.166,185.379],[185.425,185.699],[185.731,185.859],[185.899,186.099],[186.199,186.5],[186.759,187.539],[187.585,187.939],[188.006,188.339],[188.387,188.579],[188.69